<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Signal Wire</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #120f12;
      --surface: rgba(25, 22, 25, 0.88);
      --surface-alt: rgba(42, 29, 23, 0.86);
      --text: #f8f1eb;
      --muted: rgba(248, 241, 235, 0.74);
      --line: rgba(255, 173, 109, 0.2);
      --accent: #ffad6d;
      --accent-strong: #ff7a3d;
      --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 18% 8%, rgba(255, 173, 109, 0.22), transparent 18rem),
        radial-gradient(circle at 84% 0%, rgba(255, 122, 61, 0.18), transparent 16rem),
        linear-gradient(135deg, #3a2214 0%, #121116 58%, #201612 100%);
    }
    a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .shell { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      background: rgba(18, 15, 18, 0.8);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .topbar-inner,
    .footer-box {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 18px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .brand span { color: var(--accent); }
    .nav, .footer-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(280px, 0.82fr);
      gap: 22px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 72px 0 24px;
    }
    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: rgba(255, 173, 109, 0.08);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 16px;
      font-size: clamp(42px, 7vw, 84px);
      line-height: 0.94;
    }
    .lead {
      max-width: 620px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
    }
    .buttons { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 0 16px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .button.primary {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--accent-strong) 100%);
      border-color: transparent;
      color: #25120a;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .card, .panel, .footer-box {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      background: var(--surface);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .panel { padding: 22px; }
    .panel-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 16px;
    }
    .panel-item {
      padding: 12px;
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface-alt);
    }
    .panel-item strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      color: var(--accent);
    }
    section { padding: 22px 0; }
    .section-head {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: end;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .section-head h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    }
    .section-head p,
    .card p,
    .footer-box p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .card { padding: 20px; }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 21px;
    }
    .bulletins { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .bulletin {
      padding-top: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .bulletin:first-child { padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
    .footer-wrap { padding: 26px 0 60px; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero, .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .topbar-inner, .section-head, .footer-box { display: block; }
      .nav, .footer-nav { margin-top: 14px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="shell topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">Signal <span>Wire</span></a>
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#network">Network</a>
        <a href="#delivery">Delivery</a>
        <a href="#bulletin">Bulletin</a>
        <a href="#footer">Overview</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="top" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Signal infrastructure and managed delivery paths</span>
        <h1>Traffic-aware service layers for compact private systems.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Signal Wire maintains fast, low-profile delivery surfaces for teams that need
          repeatable rollout patterns, stable access paths, and clear operator notices.
        </p>
        <div class="buttons">
          <a class="button primary" href="#network">Explore network</a>
          <a class="button" href="#bulletin">Service bulletin</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <strong>Traffic note</strong>
        <p>Current public surfaces remain in standard mode. Planned route reviews are grouped into short windows with fallback capacity preserved.</p>
        <div class="panel-grid">
          <div class="panel-item"><strong>4</strong>delivery lanes</div>
          <div class="panel-item"><strong>12h</strong>bulletin refresh</div>
          <div class="panel-item"><strong>3-step</strong>rollout path</div>
          <div class="panel-item"><strong>Low</strong>public noise target</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="network">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Network services</h2>
        <p>The layout reads like a maintained infrastructure vendor site while staying lightweight enough for a single static template.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Ingress review</h3>
          <p>Public-facing route review and certificate-safe ingress maintenance for small deployments.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Path continuity</h3>
          <p>Stable delivery paths, fallback-aware updates, and controlled service exposure.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Operator notes</h3>
          <p>Short, dated bulletins that make the surface feel active without revealing internal implementation detail.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="delivery">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Delivery model</h2>
        <p>Signal Wire groups support around predictable change windows, public notices, and small operational footprints.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p>Recommended changes are bundled into reviewable windows, public copy stays brief, and service-facing guidance is written for continuity rather than marketing volume.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="bulletin">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Service bulletin</h2>
        <p>A simple bulletin list creates credibility and clickability without requiring extra pages.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card bulletins">
        <div class="bulletin">
          <strong>April bulletin</strong>
          <p>Expanded the maintenance note format to include rollout timing and fallback reminders.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bulletin">
          <strong>March bulletin</strong>
          <p>Reduced duplicate status notices across mirrored delivery surfaces.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bulletin">
          <strong>February bulletin</strong>
          <p>Refreshed route-aware access language for smaller operator environments.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <div id="footer" class="footer-wrap shell">
    <div class="footer-box">
      <div>
        <strong>Signal Wire</strong>
        <p>Managed delivery surfaces and traffic-aware support for small, distributed systems.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#top">Top</a>
        <a href="#network">Network</a>
        <a href="#delivery">Delivery</a>
        <a href="#bulletin">Bulletin</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
